      "description": "Watch St. Truiden vs Lommel United highlights and goals from Jupiler Pro League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on September 4, 2026. The Jupiler Pro League provided a thrilling spectacle on September 4, 2026 , as St. Truiden hosted Union SG . Both teams entered the pitch with high ambitions, setting the stage for a tactical battle under the floodlights of a charged stadium. The Breakthrough in the First Half The match began with high physical intensity, as both sides vied for dominance in the middle of the park. The early tension boiled over in the 21st minute when Union SG defender Kevin Mac Allister received a yellow card. Exploiting the momentary lapse in the visitors' concentration, St. Truiden struck just two minutes later. In the 23rd minute, Mateo Biondic turned provider, delivering a precise pass to Louis Patris , who clinicaly found the back of the net to give the hosts the lead. The remainder of the first half was a disciplined affair, with St. Truiden heading into the tunnel with a narrow advantage. Second Half Drama and Quick Responses The second period started with a flurry of disciplinary actions, as Abdoulaye Sissako , Robert-Jan Vanwesemael , and Nelson Ishiwatari all entered the referee's book within ten minutes of the restart. Amidst the rising tension, Union SG found an equalizer in the 56th minute. Besfort Zeneli showcased his creative flair by assisting Kevin Mac Allister , who powered home a shot to level the score at 1-1. However, the celebrations for the visitors were short-lived. St. Truiden responded with immediate clinical efficiency. In the 63rd minute, the formidable Mateo Biondic recorded his second assist of the match, setting up Relebohile Mofokeng . The attacker made no mistake, restoring St. Truiden 's lead and sending the home fans into a frenzy. Closing Stages and Tactical Changes As the clock ticked down, both managers turned to their benches to influence the final outcome. St. Truiden introduced the likes of Darius Olaru and Rob Schoofs to stabilize the midfield and protect their slim lead. Union SG pushed forward, bringing on Raul Florucz in the 79th minute to spark a late comeback, but the home defense remained resolute. After three minutes of stoppage time, the final whistle blew, confirming a hard-fought victory for St. Truiden in a match defined by swift counter-attacks and individual brilliance."
